/-
# Two-generated direct powers of finite simple groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 17.116)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.116 (A. Erfanian, J. Wiegold): let `n(G)`
be the maximum of positive integers `n` such that the `n`-th direct power of a finite simple group
`G` is 2-generated. Is it true that `n(G) ≥ √|G|`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple
public import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SimpleGroupDirectPowerTwoGeneratedKourovka17Problem116Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.116 (A.
Erfanian, J. Wiegold). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701417 (`KOU-17.116`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath
v1.8.0.

The problem concerns non-abelian simple groups: for `G` cyclic of prime order `p`, `Gⁿ` is
2-generated only for `n ≤ 2 < √p` when `p ≥ 5`. The target is the stronger bound of the resolution,
`n(G) > 2√|G|`, written as: some `n` with `4|G| < n²` has `Gⁿ = Fin n → G` generated by two
elements. Since `Gⁿ` maps onto `Gᵐ` for `m ≤ n`, this is the bound for the maximum `n(G)`.
-/

/-- **Kourovka Problem 17.116 (two-generated direct powers of simple groups).** The statement, in
the form of its resolution, that for every non-abelian finite simple group $G$ there is a natural
number $n$ with $n^2 > 4|G|$, that is, $n > 2\sqrt{|G|}$, such that the direct power $G^n$ is
generated by two elements. The problem is due to A. Erfanian and J. Wiegold.

Since $G^n$ maps onto $G^m$ for $m \le n$, this says that the largest $n(G)$ such that $G^{n(G)}$ is
2-generated satisfies $n(G) > 2\sqrt{|G|}$. -/
def directPowerTwoGeneratedBound : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G], IsSimpleGroup G → (∃ a b : G, a * b ≠ b * a) →
    ∃ n : ℕ, 4 * Nat.card G < n ^ 2 ∧ ∃ x y : Fin n → G, Subgroup.closure {x, y} = ⊤

/--
**Maróti–Tamburini bound for two-generated direct powers.** For every non-abelian finite simple
group $G$ there is a natural number $n$ with $n^2 > 4|G|$, that is, $n > 2\sqrt{|G|}$, such that
the direct power $G^n$ is generated by two elements. This answers Kourovka Problem 17.116
positively.

Maróti and Tamburini (Theorem 1.1) prove $2\sqrt{|G|} < h(G)$ for every non-abelian finite simple
group $G$, where $h(G)$ is the largest $n$ such that $G^n$ is 2-generated; writing $n(G)$ for this
same $h(G)$, the Kourovka Archive answers 17.116 "Yes, it is, even with $n(G) > 2\sqrt{|G|}$".

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D.
Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 17.116 (A. Erfanian, J. Wiegold);
resolution: A. Maróti and M. C. Tamburini Bellani, A solution to a problem of Wiegold, Comm. Algebra
41 (2013), 34-49, Theorem 1.1 (for any non-abelian finite simple group G, 2√|G| < h(G), the largest
n with G^n 2-generated); Kourovka Archive, Problem 17.116 (Yes, it is, even with n(G) > 2√|G|),
https://www.renyi.hu/~maroti/centralizer12.pdf.
-/
public theorem_wanted directPowerTwoGeneratedBound_holds : directPowerTwoGeneratedBound

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.SimpleGroupDirectPowerTwoGeneratedKourovka17Problem116Wanted
